---
description: Slurm submit scripts default --requeue on mit_preemptable
globs: scripts/submit*.sh
alwaysApply: true
---

# Slurm submit defaults (`mit_preemptable`)

Every `scripts/submit_*.sh` that calls `sbatch` (or wraps one that does) must:

1. Set `PARTITION` (default `pi_fiete`) before sourcing defaults.
2. Source `scripts/sbatch_defaults.sh`.
3. Pass `$SBATCH_EXTRA` to **every** `sbatch` (`sbatch --parsable $SBATCH_EXTRA ...`).

`PARTITION=mit_preemptable` or `mit_preem` defaults `SBATCH_EXTRA=--requeue`.
Do not hardcode `--requeue` or `SBATCH_EXTRA="${SBATCH_EXTRA:---requeue}"`.
Explicit `SBATCH_EXTRA=""` disables it. Do not submit from the agent (see no-orcd-access).
